<article class="env-lemma" id="0384">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0384">Lemma <span data-tag="0384">33.6.6</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. Let $x \in X$ be a point, and let $x' \in X_{k'}$ be a point lying over $x$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ is geometrically reduced at $x$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X_{k'}$ is geometrically reduced at $x'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In particular, $X$ is geometrically reduced over $k$ if and only if $X_{k'}$ is geometrically reduced over $k'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that (1) implies (2). Assume (2). Let $k''/k$ be a finite purely inseparable field extension and let $x'' \in X_{k''}$ be a point lying over $x$ (actually it is unique). Choose a common field extension $k'''/k$ of $k''/k$ and $k'/k$, see Fields, Lemma <a href="/tag/0H7K" data-tag="0H7K">9.6.9</a>. Choose a point $x''' \in X_{k'''}$ lying over both $x'$ and $x''$. Consider the map of local rings 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_{X_{k''}, x''} \longrightarrow \mathcal{O}_{X_{k'''}, x'''}.  \]
</div>
    <p>
       This is a flat local ring homomorphism and hence faithfully flat. By (2) we see that the local ring on the right is reduced. Thus by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/033F" data-tag="033F">10.164.2</a> we conclude that $\mathcal{O}_{X_{k''}, x''}$ is reduced. Thus by Lemma <a href="/tag/035Y" data-tag="035Y">33.6.5</a> we conclude that $X$ is geometrically reduced at $x$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>